# Per-experiment embedding ablation indices (issue #174 / scripts/run_embedding_ablation.py).
# Multi-GB per model and reproducible from the selected fixture/private corpus
# via the runner; the committed evidence lives in docs/embedding-ablation.md.
data/embedding-ablation/
# Per-experiment embedding ablation eval outputs (issue #389 / scripts/run_embedding_ablation.py).
# eval_summary.json + traces/ per model; reproducible from the selected corpus.
# Headline numbers are committed in docs/embedding-ablation.md so the public repo
# stays small (the raw JSON is ~2 MB per model and traces/ adds another ~2 MB).
reports/embedding-ablation/
# LoRA fine-tuning training pairs (issue #433 / scripts/generate_finetune_pairs.py).
# Generated from the fixture/private corpus via the script; the 5k-scale
# embedding_pairs.jsonl is reproducible with `seed=17`. data/training/sample.jsonl is the committed
# schema reference (~25 representative rows).
data/training/*
!data/training/sample.jsonl
# LoRA fine-tuning notebook artifacts (issue #435 / notebooks/embedding_finetune.ipynb).
# `lora_adapter/` is the trained PEFT delta (~30 MB) — distributed via HF Hub,
# not committed. `notebooks/_artifacts/` holds the training curve PNG and any
# other run outputs that should accompany the writeup on the model card, not
# the repo.
lora_adapter/
notebooks/_artifacts/
# M2 (#207): vectors live in a sidecar .npy file alongside index.json so
# the JSON stays small and a future VectorStore abstraction (#176) can
# swap backends. Both files together are the portfolio sample.
!data/index/embeddings.npy
outputs/*
!outputs/answer.json
reports/*
reports/real*/
reports/**/*.local.json
reports/**/*.jsonl
reports/**/*.parquet
reports/**/*.sqlite
reports/**/*.sqlite3
reports/**/*.db
# Aggregate-only artifacts under reports/real100/ are committable
# (ADR 0005 commit boundary). The negation chain below allowlists
# only the explicit aggregate filenames — eval_summary.json and any
# per-case trace stay ignored.
!reports/real100/
reports/real100/*
!reports/real100/baseline.aggregate.json
# Issue #896 — real-100 corpus EDA aggregate (script:
# scripts/eda_real100.py). 4-axis profile of metadata / chunks /
# text_source / eval-cross. ADR 0005 boundary preserved by the script
# (no doc/chunk IDs or raw text; agencies past rank 10 anonymized).
!reports/real100/eda.md
!reports/real100/eda.aggregate.json
!reports/real100/history/
reports/real100/history/*
!reports/real100/history/*.aggregate.json
# Issue #897 — RAG pipeline EDA aggregate (script:
# scripts/rag_pipeline_eda.py). 7-axis pipeline-dynamics profile derived
# from eval_summary.json::case_results. Two surfaces:
#   - reports/rag_pipeline.* (public fixture smoke / local pipeline aggregate)
#   - reports/real100/rag_pipeline.* (private/internal real eval, ADR 0005)
# ADR 0005 boundary preserved by the script (no case IDs, chunk IDs, or
# raw text; retry reason prefixes only).
!reports/rag_pipeline.md
!reports/rag_pipeline.aggregate.json
!reports/real100/rag_pipeline.md
!reports/real100/rag_pipeline.aggregate.json
# Issue #945 — distinguishing-power gauge aggregate (script:
# scripts/distinguishing_power.py, ADR 0053 §Consequences gauge).
# Reads eval_summary.json::ablation.runs, emits (default - floor) /
# (1 - floor) per metric. Aggregate-only (no per-case data); ADR 0005
# boundary preserved by the gauge formula itself.
!reports/real100/distinguishing_power.md
!reports/real100/distinguishing_power.aggregate.json
# Issue #969 — trajectory-rationality judge aggregate (ADR 0056, script:
# scripts/run_rationality_judge.py). Reads eval_summary.json + per-case
# trace JSON, emits 3-axis mean + 95% bootstrap CI + effective_n.
# Aggregate-only (no per-case rationale text or trace data); per-case
# payload at rationality.local.json stays ignored under reports/real100/*.
!reports/real100/rationality.md
!reports/real100/rationality.aggregate.json
# Issue #1002 — failure-mode distribution dashboard (ADR 0059 Phase 5
# supply 2, script: scripts/render_failure_distribution.py). Reads
# eval_summary.json::failure_category_counts (top-level) + abstention_outcomes,
# emits 7-category composition table + ADR 0059 first-match contract check.
# Aggregate-only (no per-case data); the renderer is a read-only consumer
# of the surface introduced by ADR 0059 (PR #1001).
!reports/real100/failure_distribution.md
!reports/real100/failure_distribution.aggregate.json
# Issue #1243 — per-category failure-mode slices (script:
# scripts/render_failure_slices.py). Per-case decomposition of the ADR 0059
# failure surface for audit verifiability (retrieval-miss-inspection.md).
# Aggregate-only — counts/cardinalities only, no query/answer text, doc_id,
# or chunk_id; raw eval_summary.json::case_results stays ignored (line 95).
!reports/real100/failure_slices.aggregate.json
# verifier_false_negative overlap inspection (script:
# scripts/render_verifier_false_negative_overlap.py). Aggregate-only
# counts/buckets for retrieval/citation/unsupported overlap; raw
# eval_summary.json::case_results stays ignored.
!reports/real100/verifier_false_negative_overlap.aggregate.json
# Multi-chunk evidence failure analysis (script:
# scripts/render_multi_chunk_evidence_failures.py). Aggregate-only
# counts/buckets over gold/retrieved chunk diagnostics; raw
# eval_summary.json::case_results stays ignored.
!reports/real100/multi_chunk_evidence_failures.aggregate.json
# Difficulty profiler (script: scripts/render_difficulty_profile.py).
# Aggregate-only buckets and means over private real-eval difficulty slices;
# raw eval_summary.json::case_results and index chunk text stay ignored.
!reports/real100/difficulty_profile.md
!reports/real100/difficulty_profile.aggregate.json
# Multi-chunk retrieval strategy decision (script:
# scripts/render_multi_chunk_retrieval_strategy.py). Aggregate-only decision
# over the multi-chunk evidence failure aggregate; no raw case rows.
!reports/real100/multi_chunk_retrieval_strategy.aggregate.json
